<title>USA: Deutsche Bank expands US base metals team.</title>
<headline>Deutsche Bank expands US base metals team.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Deutsche Bank said it has expanded its base metals operation in North America with the addition of Michael Turek at its New York location.</p>
<p>Turek previously ran Lehman's metal desk for 14 years.</p>
<p>&quot;Deutsche Bank has increasingly expanded its base metal personnel and product range in a strategy aimed at becoming a dominant metal dealer,&quot; the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>Deutsche Bank is a ring dealing member of the London Metal Exchange through its Deutsche Sharps Pixley subsidiary.</p>
<p>((New York Commodity Desk 212-859-1646))</p>
</text>
